# Ask Matt Workflow

## When to Use

- The next workflow/skill is unclear.
- A request could fit multiple paths (planned feature, ad-hoc task, testing, architecture, release, hard bug).

## Core Approach

Read and follow `.agents/skills/ask-matt/SKILL.md` exactly.

Routing highlights:

- Recommend a **gate tier** first (`gate:mechanical | standard | full` — ADR 0012) when implementing
- Planned feature -> `to-prd` then `to-issues` (assign `gate:*` + blocks)
- Something's broken (hard bug) -> `diagnosing-bugs`
- Ad-hoc fix now (no ticket) -> classify gate -> `implement` (+ `tdd` when appropriate)
- Agreed spec ready to build -> `implement`
- Design ambiguity -> `grill-with-docs`
- Stale framework / library instructions -> `upstream-brief`
- Vocabulary/shape problems -> `domain-modeling` / `codebase-design`
- Runnable validation required -> `prototype` (+ `handoff` if crossing sessions)
- Jest/Playwright work -> matching test workflow (mechanical may skip specialist hops)
- Release preparation -> `release-and-deploy-workflow`
- Review branch or WIP changes -> `code-review` (optional for mechanical)

